I am in the kitchen at the office.
It is time for a break.
I am getting myself a coffee.
My colleague Nele also comes into the kitchen.
We often work together.
Nele smiles in greeting.
We talk a bit about our project.
Then she tells me about her plans for the weekend.
"I am cooking a big dinner on Friday," Nele says.
"I would love to invite you to my place."
I am a little surprised, but I am very happy.
"I hope that you have time," she says.
I thank her for the nice invitation.
"Yes, I do not have anything planned for Friday evening yet," I answer.
"I will definitely come!"
Nele beams and takes her cup.
"We will certainly have a lot of fun," she says.
I think that it will be a nice evening.
I am glad that we are getting to know each other better.
I go back to my desk with my coffee.
